# 4. Step 0 — Verify the Cluster

Before Docker or Kubernetes deployment work, verify that the cluster is reachable.

```bash
export PROJECT_ID="devops-project-503113"
export REGION="europe-west1"
export CLUSTER_NAME="devsecops-gke"
```

Configure `kubectl`:

```bash
gcloud container clusters get-credentials "$CLUSTER_NAME" \
  --region "$REGION" \
  --project "$PROJECT_ID"
```

Check the context:

```bash
kubectl config current-context
```

Expected context should reference:

```text
devops-project-503113
europe-west1
devsecops-gke
```

Check nodes:

```bash
kubectl get nodes -o wide
```

Worker nodes should eventually show:

```text
STATUS
Ready
```

Check system workloads:

```bash
kubectl get pods -A
```

Useful diagnostic:

```bash
kubectl cluster-info
```

Do not continue to application deployment if the Kubernetes API itself is unreachable.

