# 7. Step 3 — Run the Container Locally

Before Kubernetes, prove that the container itself works.

Example if the application listens on container port `8080`:

```bash
docker run --rm \
  -p 8080:8080 \
  "${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG}"
```

From another terminal:

```bash
curl -v http://127.0.0.1:8080/
```

Replace ports according to your application.

The important distinction is:

```text
Docker problem?
or
Kubernetes problem?
```

If the image does not work with plain Docker, Kubernetes normally will not fix the application.

