# 8. Step 4 — Run Basic Security Checks

These commands are useful before pushing an image.

## Gitleaks

From the repository root:

```bash
gitleaks detect \
  --source . \
  --redact
```

Purpose:

```text
Source repository
      |
      v
Search for accidentally committed secrets
```

Examples:

- API keys
- private keys
- tokens
- passwords
- cloud credentials

## Trivy filesystem scan

```bash
trivy fs \
  --severity HIGH,CRITICAL \
  .
```

## Trivy image scan

```bash
trivy image \
  --severity HIGH,CRITICAL \
  "${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG}"
```

Later Jenkins will automate these steps.

For the learning phase, run them manually so you understand what CI will eventually do.

