# 61. Troubleshooting Cheat Sheet

## Kubernetes API timeout

```bash
kubectl cluster-info
```

Refresh credentials:

```bash
gcloud container clusters get-credentials "$CLUSTER_NAME" \
  --region "$REGION" \
  --project "$PROJECT_ID"
```

Also check GKE authorized networks if your admin public IP changed.

## No nodes

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

Check node pool:

```bash
gcloud container node-pools describe \
  devsecops-gke-primary \
  --cluster devsecops-gke \
  --region europe-west1 \
  --project devops-project-503113
```

## `Pending` Pod

```bash
kubectl describe pod -n staging <POD>
```

Look for `FailedScheduling`.

## `ImagePullBackOff`

```bash
kubectl describe pod -n staging <POD>
```

Check:

```text
image reference
ECR repository
imagePullSecret
namespace
ECR auth expiration
IAM permissions
```

## `CrashLoopBackOff`

```bash
kubectl logs -n staging <POD>
kubectl logs -n staging <POD> --previous
```

## Service does not work

```bash
kubectl get pods -n staging --show-labels
kubectl get svc webapp -n staging -o yaml
```

Compare Pod labels with Service selector.

